y outranks an older committed vbal) is recorded together with my reason for rejecting it, namely that vbal records the ballot at which a value was accepted while a fresh ballot carries none, and that the ignored reply reports the one status the protocol treats as final. Limitations keep the derived-field oracle, the harness-literal identity, and the out-of-scope consequences (accept-round completion, execution divergence) visible as independent questions.\\n\\nThe finding is therefore scoped and reviewable: in the declared configuration the recovering replica does not adopt a reply that reports the instance COMMITTED, and the wider consequences remain separate questions rather than part of the reviewed proposition. No map object was changed and no requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
